<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy" %>
<div class="wide-container legal-page">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">Last updated November 23, 2026</p>

  <p>
    This policy explains what information Ardesian, LLC ("we", "us") collects when you use
    ardesian.com and the Buddy app for iPhone, what we do with it, and who else sees it. It covers the
    website, its subdomains, and the Buddy app.
  </p>

  <p>
    We use your information to run the site for you and for the people you choose to share things
    with. We don't sell it, we don't use it for advertising, and we don't use it to track you across
    other apps or websites.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Your account</h3>
  <p>
    When you create an account, we store your username and password. Your password is stored as a
    one-way hash, so we can't see it. If you add a phone number or email address, we store those too.
    If you start using the site before creating an account, we make a guest account that your browser
    remembers until you give it a username and password.
  </p>

  <h3>What you enter</h3>
  <p>
    We store everything you enter on the site, including lists, agenda items, timers, chores, notes,
    logged events, answers to prompts, automations, and messages to Buddy along with any photos or
    files you attach.
  </p>

  <h3>The Buddy app</h3>
  <p>
    The Buddy app sends your phone's battery level and whether it's charging. Everything else in this
    section is off until you allow it in the Buddy app, which is when iOS asks for your permission.
    After that you can turn each one on or off from your device's page on the site, or in the
    iPhone's Settings, at any time.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Your precise location when it changes significantly, the places
      you arrive at and leave, and when you enter or leave places you've saved.</li>
    <li><strong>Workouts and fitness (Apple Health):</strong> Each workout's type, start and end
      times, duration, calories, distance, and heart rate. If you turn them on, it also sends daily
      totals for steps, active energy, exercise minutes, and sleep. The app only reads from Apple
      Health and never writes to it.</li>
    <li><strong>Calendar, reminders, and contacts:</strong> Events, reminders, and contacts on your
      phone when they're added, changed, or removed.</li>
    <li><strong>Bluetooth accessories:</strong> The battery level of connected accessories that report
      one.</li>
    <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> A push token so we can send notifications to your phone.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The app also sends your phone's name, model, iOS version, app version, and time zone so you can
    see and sign out your devices from the site. When you share something to Buddy from another app,
    like a photo, a place, or a link, we receive what you shared.
  </p>

  <h3>Services you link</h3>
  <p>
    If you link another service to your account, we only receive what that service provides for the
    feature you turned on. You can unlink it at any time.
  </p>

  <h3>Logs</h3>
  <p>
    Our server keeps standard request logs, including your IP address, browser or app version, the
    page requested, and the time. We use these to keep the site secure and to fix problems.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To show you your data and do what you ask, including lists, the agenda, timers,
      notifications, and the automations you set up.</li>
    <li>To let Buddy reply to you. When you message Buddy, your message and the information Buddy
      needs to answer it (for example your agenda, a list, your location, or a recent workout) are
      sent to an AI provider to write the reply.</li>
    <li>To keep the site running and secure, and to fix problems when they come up.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell or rent your personal information, and we don't share it with advertisers or data
    brokers. We do use the following services to run the site, and each one only receives what it
    needs for its part:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> and <strong>Anthropic</strong>, to write Buddy's replies.</li>
    <li><strong>Amazon Web Services</strong>, to store uploaded files and photos and to send
      email.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong>, for maps and address lookups.</li>
    <li><strong>Twilio</strong>, to send text messages if you've added a phone number.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple</strong>, to deliver notifications to the Buddy app.</li>
    <li><strong>Slack</strong>, to alert us when something breaks. These alerts can include your
      username and details about the error.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also share information when required by law or to protect the safety of people using the
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>Health data</h2>
  <p>
    Information from Apple Health is only used to log your workouts and totals to your account, and
    for any automations or Buddy features you set up with it. We don't use it for advertising,
    marketing, or data mining, and we don't sell it or share it beyond what's described in this
    policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing with other people</h2>
  <p>
    When you share something on the site, like a list, an agenda, or chores with the people you live
    with, those people can see it and make changes based on the access you've given them. Nothing
    else in your account is visible to other users.
  </p>
  <p>
    We have access to the data stored on our server, and we only look at it when something needs to
    be fixed, when you ask for help, or when the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your data for as long as you have an account. You can delete most things yourself on the
    site. If you'd like to close your account and delete everything in it, email us at the address
    below. Your data is removed from the site right away and from our backups as they're replaced.
  </p>
  <p>
    In the Buddy app, turning a feature off stops it from sending anything new. Signing a phone out
    from the <%= link_to "Buddy App Devices", app_devices_path %> page on the site disconnects it
    immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    All data is sent over encrypted connections, passwords are stored as hashes, and each phone signs
    in with its own token. That token is kept in the iPhone's Keychain and can be revoked from the
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site and the app aren't intended for children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their
    personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see, correct, export, or delete your information at any time by emailing us. We'll
    respond within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we'll post the updated version here and update the date at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about this policy, email us at <%= mail_to "contact@ardesian.com" %> or
    visit the <%= link_to "Support", support_path %> page.
  </p>
</div>
